  "final_message": "If you call `retry.call_with_retry()` without passing `max_attempts`, it makes at most 4 attempts, and that count includes the first try.\n\n- In `retry.py`, `DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4`. When `max_attempts` is `None`, the loop `for _ in range(attempts)` runs that many times.\n- Each pass calls `fn()` and returns as soon as one succeeds. If all 4 fail, it raises the last exception it caught.\n- `main7.py` calls it with no `max_attempts`, so it uses this default.\n- `retry.py` doesn't import `decoy_network.MAX_RETRIES = 3` or `decoy_backoff.RETRY_LIMIT = 5`, so neither affects the answer.\n- `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` has nothing to do with retries.\n\nANSWER: 4",
